			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820658">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Formatting: short experimentation log to go over the lab testing of the anomaly and then there will be a classified email followed by a field log going over MTF using the anomalous instances.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: anomalous trait in 0.01% of the domesticated cats in the world that allows them to see and reveal incorporeal entities that can't be seen. After initial testing gets approval for trying to find field applications for use by Mu-13 “ghost busters”</p>
<p>Central Narrative: researcher in the Department of Spectral Phenomena is surprised to see the invisible entity she is working on when she brings her cat into the observation room.</p>
<p>The cat is approved to see for further interaction between invisible entities. it is put into the contain cell of friendly specter and shows capability to see and reveal the entity to a D-Class.</p>
<p>More cats are intercepted from veterinarian clinics and shelters within the following months.</p>
<p>A level 4 clearance email can be read with the researcher asking for O5 approval on field tests with the cats by MTF Mu-13 with similar entities because current foundation equipment in some cases can go through electrical malfunctions. where in the cats precisely track and reveal the entity.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A field log shows Mu-13 members Gilligan and Alex field testing SCP-XXXX-1 and SCP-XXXX-2 when they go to retrieve a specter living inside an old warehouse that was located by foundation agents in a routine myth investigation. Gilligan is adamant about treating them like foundation equipment and alex treats them like cats.</p>
<p>They split up when they enter the warehosue. Gilligan has a hard time getting Grompy to respond to the cold way he delivers his commands. Alex is experiencing good results with Fred who is highly responsive too her kindly manner and begins leading her with his lease.</p>
<p>Fred experiences a piloerection and hisses alerting alex of a shelving unit about to fall onto them. Fred then begins to pull on the lease into the direction of a door to a workshop.</p>
<p>Alex radios for Gil who has to pick grompy up and run. Gil complains that the cat doesn't listen to him, alex suggests kinder words.</p>
<p>entering the room both cats start to lead them to a part of the room when gil gives grompy some encouraging commands. then they encounter the entity, the cats and the MTf cornering it and using temporarily containment devices.</p>
<p>Cute cats seeing ghosts</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

