<p>Hey again!</p>
<p>So it sounds like if the cats are alone, they can interact with the entities, but if there's a person then the entity attacks them instead of the cat. To be honest, I'm not really too keen on this part of the concept (cats attacking dimensional entities). Just having them able to see ghosts and the like is enough.</p>
<p>Onto the narrative though, this could work with SCP-126 (as in a cute interaction). However, I feel a civilian incident, with Mu-13 investigating a house or apartment for anomalous activity and being saved by a cat, would also work. You can decide which one you'd like in your article.</p>
<p>Last thing I'd suggest is that you contact someone on the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> for some more crit and alternative opinions.</p>
<p>Hope this helps!</p>

