			<div class="content" id="post-content-4821196">
									

<p>I got summoned by IRC Chat. Let's crit this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This has potential to be a very cute article. My only concern is that the interaction with SCP-126 might be seen as &quot;trying to be interesting by hanging on the popularity of a Series I article&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A level 4 clearance email can be read with the researcher asking for O5 approval on field application for MTF Mu-13 and after approval a field test log provides a somewhat assuming account of their first field mission and the interactions between the MTF and the Cats</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I suggest focusing on the adventures of the cat helping out the MFT. And you should write your own ghostly character as to avoid using any other SCPs. What happens during this time? Does the cat helps with an uncontained ghost? Does the cat helps on a containment breach? Also, how does the cat <em>reacts</em>? Is it hostile or docile towards ghosts? Does the cat helps on other things apart from locating the ghosts? Cats are very intelligent animals, so you could play with what the cat does during its time with the MTF. Is it playful, arrogant, curious&#8230;? What is the point of view of the MTF members over having a cat to help them?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I like this concept, and it can be developed on a good way, but you need to explain more what happens during the central narrative.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look!</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Here, have a Placeholder for a follow-up. I'll crit this within 24 hours.</span></p>
<p>I got some unexpected IRL stuff, so sorry for being more than 24 hrs late since I received your PM.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;more&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>using an experimentation log</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I suggest keeping this log somewhat short. This anomaly seems more focused towards how the Foundation uses it than how it itself works. Maybe just some lines about &quot;after analyzing the cat, it was discovered that the ability comes from an anomalous gen that is present on 0.01% of the cats&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A level 4 clearance email can be read with the researcher asking for O5 approval on field application</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm unsure about this. I mean, not <em>this</em>, but instead the background that this carries. Surely the Foundation has some way to track ghosts, so the readers will surely ask themselves &quot;Why using cats instead of Foundation technology?&quot;</p>
<p>You need to answer this question during this email exchange. Maybe it's because of budget? Maybe it's because cats are more loyal than some machines? Maybe because they're more fickle?</p>
<p>Now, your field log seems to have too many characters (6, with the cats, of course), and the only &quot;imposrtant&quot; thing that happens is that one of the cats alerts the team before the ghoost attacks? I would suggest adding more scenes to this log. Maybe their struggles to control the cats or some spooky/slappy occurrences before the ghost attacks?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, you might need to explain some background things, but this could be a great article.</p>

							</div>

								
