<p>So mostly I am on board with this. But there a few things I think need work:</p>
<p>1) layout: how is your article to be structured? How will you communicate these things to your reader logistically? If it were a tale this is easy, but as an SCP, you have to not only follow formatting but also use the formatting in an engaging way. For example, I dislike endless journal entries unless they are written in a punchy and interesting way&#8230; the same goes for test logs.</p>
<p>2) I am a cat person, so take this with love&#8230;. but I can't imagine a cat doing what its told if its life depended on it. So these cats can see spectral entities&#8230; but how could the MTF or field researchers utilize the cats to do so? Not like cats are gonna be responding to voice commands the way dogs usually do&#8230; unless they were trained dramatically I'd guess.</p>
<p>3) perspective: Who's perspective is this from? As cute as the cats are, it will be hard to relate to the cats as characters</p>

