<p>Thank you for your review!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">here&nbsp;is&nbsp;my&nbsp;feedback</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Thanks&nbsp;again</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>1) I realized I didn't go over the layout much in this post. it was going to contain a brief containment procedure and description and then it was going to have an initial experiment log that I was going to use the experiment log format style I found. then use an email exchange and then I was going to try to make the field log be the longest part of this article and go over the team of three using those three cats to locate and catch a hostile entity. I have it already formatted in what I think is a decent way on my draft but was hoping once I get approved to post a draft get more feed back there. I really enjoy the sandbox formatting and would love some tips and advice.</p>
<p>2) in my draft I have it that the cat with experience a piloerection in its tail and begin to growl while following the entity with its eyes and this would alert the MTF to its presents. I have also thought around in my draft about the cats being able to seek specters out if they are in a certain amount of distance from them. I guess you might relate them to how Ghost hunter shows misuse EMF readers too find ghosts but these would actually work. I also have thought about if the cats are looking at the ghost then it gets revealed to be seen by the human eye, but I felt that would not go over well as it might sound ridiculous.</p>
<p>3) as for perspective I was going with the three MTF members Commander Gilligan, Alex, and Henry and their different interactions with the cats. Gilligan who treats them like hardware and is paired with SCP-XXXX-Fred, Alex who treats them like they are cute cats and is paired with SCP-XXXX-Grompy, and Henry who hates the cats and is paired with SCP-XXXX-Mittens, he is more of a dog person. I am working on ways in my draft to give the cats more personality, but am still deciding on how I want each of the cats to act differently with their respected &quot;supervisor&quot;</p>
<p>I will edit my idea forum post to reflect the great advice you gave me.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

